From e244803a0d5752396411729c5435e91b96b70bfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:40:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] tvOS: the system keyboard for text entry

#118332 leaves text entry as a TODO: tvOS won't bring up its keyboard
for UIKeyInput views or an uneditable UITextView. A hidden UITextField
now stands in for the input view on tvOS, so DisplayServer's virtual
keyboard (a LineEdit being edited) brings up the system keyboard. Its
text is mirrored into Godot as key events, the LineEdit's maximum
length is respected, and dismissing the keyboard with Menu stops the
LineEdit editing.

The field is from closed pull request #123885's continuation (the
tvos-port branch of sanarena/godot), verified there on Apple TV
hardware.

Test: on an Apple TV, selecting a LineEdit brings up the keyboard,
typing appears in the LineEdit, and Menu closes the keyboard and stops
editing.

Upstream: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123885
